302	
303	    // === YOUR SCRIPTS BELOW (use var for top-level variables, define onThemeChange for chart re-renders) ===
304	  </script>
305	</body>
306	</html>
307	```
308	
309	### Skeleton Rules
310	
311	**Do:**
312	- Use `var` for all top-level variables (avoids TDZ errors when functions are hoisted)
313	- Use `data-reveal` attribute on sections/cards for scroll animation
314	- Use `data-count="77" data-suffix="%"` for animated number counters
315	- Use `.animate.delay-N` classes for page-load entrance animations
316	- Use CSS `:hover` for hover effects (baked into `.card` already)
317	- Define `function onThemeChange() {}` to re-render charts on theme toggle
318	- Use `<main>`, `<section>`, `<header>`, `<article>` for semantic HTML
319	- Keep all chart variables as `var` (not `let`/`const`) at script top level
320	
321	**Don't:**
322	- Don't include Motion.js unless you specifically need spring physics
323	- Don't hide content via JS/CSS for animation — use `data-reveal` pattern instead
324	- Don't use `let`/`const` for variables that might be referenced before declaration
325	- Don't use `.finished` Promise chains for sequencing — use `setTimeout`
326	- Don't put animation logic that could crash before nav/chart setup code
